{"name":"Spinach White","hex":"#e4e8da","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spinach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of species Spinacia oleracea of edible plants, or its leaves.","Any of numerous plants, or their leaves, which are used for greens in the same way Spinacia oleracea is or resemble it in some way."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spinach"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spinach","blocks":[{"text":"Spinach is a leafy green flowering plant native to Central and Western Asia. It is of the order Caryophyllales, family Amaranthaceae, subfamily Chenopodioideae. Its leaves are a common vegetable consumed either fresh, cooked or after storage. The taste differs considerably between cooked and raw: the high oxalate content may be reduced by blanching."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Spinacia_oleracea_Spinazie_bloeiend.jpg/330px-Spinacia_oleracea_Spinazie_bloeiend.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spinach","wikidata":"Q81464"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg/500px-Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg/1280px-Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg/500px-Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIllustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg/250px-Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg/330px-Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg/250px-Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloem